# Nested sub-callee with a non-input read — refused (niet-zuivere sub-callee)

A nested subscope lowers to an Invoke only when its own callee is a pure function
(PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3a, 2026-08-25). `InnerNonInput`'s output reads `helper`, an
INTERNAL variable (neither an input nor a nested subscope output), which has no
FunctionDef parameter to bind — a non-input read. So the nested composition
`KamerNested.bedrag = inner.y` refuses per element: an impure sub-callee has no
function image.

```catala
declaration scope InnerNonInput:
  input x content integer
  internal helper content integer
  output y content integer

scope InnerNonInput:
  definition helper equals 100
  definition y equals x + helper

declaration scope KamerNested:
  input grondslag content integer
  inner scope InnerNonInput
  output bedrag content integer

scope KamerNested:
  definition inner.x equals grondslag
  definition bedrag equals inner.y

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslagen content list of integer
  output totaal content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition totaal equals
    combine all b
      among (map each g among grondslagen to (output of KamerNested with { -- grondslag: g }).bedrag)
      in acc initially 0 with (acc + b)
```
